    {
      "id": "1pk5o10",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Weather vs Climate"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Köppen climate classification is an empirical system based on mean annual and monthly temperature and precipitation values.",
        "The five main climate groups are Tropical (A), Dry (B), Warm Temperate (C), Continental (D), and Polar (E).",
        "Thornthwaite's classification is a rational system based on water balance and Potential Evapotranspiration (PE).",
        "India features multiple Köppen climate zones including Amw (Western Coast), Cwg (Ganga Plains), and As (Coromandel Coast)."
      ],
      "id": "7i1p3gz"
    },
    {
