    {
      "id": "jdnmdhu",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "2. Why Do We Classify Climate?"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "q2w6nqn",
      "content": "• To understand global climatic patterns."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "nzb0u88",
      "content": "• To predict vegetation and biodiversity."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "xt043t8",
      "content": "• To assist agricultural planning."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "7x3z147",
      "content": "• To study climate change trends."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "1tcw383",
      "content": "• To simplify geographical learning."
    },
    {
      "id": "f8tsb0j",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "3. Basis of Climate Classification"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "whwzt0q",
      "content": "• Temperature"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "4boqhm0",
      "content": "• Precipitation"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "imxwmrw",
      "content": "• Seasonality"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "3o2jr2h",
      "content": "• Evaporation"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "z2cyiaz",
      "content": "• Vegetation indicators"
    },
    {
      "id": "qnm4rq7",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "4. Köppen Climate Classification – The Most Important System"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ipf8ww7",
      "content": "Developed by Wladimir Köppen, this system links climate with natural vegetation. It is the MOST widely used classification in competitive exams because it is objective and data-based."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "jvwleg5",
      "content": "Köppen used a combination of CAPITAL and small letters to describe climate characteristics."
    },
    {
