      "level": 2,
      "content": "12. Advantages of Köppen Classification"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Match Köppen codes for India: 'Amw' represents Tropical Monsoon with short dry season, while 'As' represents Monsoon with dry summer (Coromandel Coast).",
        "Distinguish Empirical (Köppen: based on observed data) vs Genetic (based on causes/air masses) climate classifications.",
        "Thornthwaite classification focuses heavily on Potential Evapotranspiration (PE) and Moisture Index."
      ],
      "id": "y3zf973"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "rn7k8mu",
      "content": "• Simple and objective."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "obicshw",
      "content": "• Closely matches vegetation zones."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "3041j14",
      "content": "• Uses measurable data."
    },
    {
      "id": "p24xos9",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "13. Limitations"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "qiw57ru",
      "content": "• Does not fully consider wind patterns."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "4ps1ty2",
      "content": "• Ignores extreme weather events."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "bok28kr",
      "content": "• Boundaries are sometimes artificial."
    },
    {
      "id": "5ln9m9y",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "MASTER EXAM POINTS"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "1wlzdus",
      "content": "• Köppen classification is vegetation-based.<br></br>• 'A' climates are tropical.<br></br>• 'B' climates are dry.<br></br>• Mediterranean climate is 'Cs'.<br></br>• Tundra is 'ET'.<br></br>• India mainly has 'Am' climate."
    }
